{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9kdid34r8","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"CASE STUDY: Self-learning KB loop — OFF 0% → ON 100% on held-out bench (overlay-save + locale-sum)","summary":"Full end-to-end validation of the self-learning loop hypothesis across two held-out bench candidates.\n\nSETUP: Agents solve from a prose spec only (no tests, no rubric). Graded externally with a held-out suite they never see. ON arm gets gated search_knowledge; OFF arm gets nothing. Candidates chosen so the correct approach is non-obvious without KB: overlay-save (must route through graph-store JSONL, not ephemeral JSON) and locale-sum (parseFloat breaks on de-DE comma-decimal — must use Intl.NumberFormat).\n\nRESULTS:\n- overlay-save: OFF 0/2 solved (edgePass 1/3 each) → ON 4/4 solved (edgePass 3/3 each)\n- locale-sum: OFF 0/5 solved (edgePass 0/8 each) → ON 3/3 confirmed-inject trials solved (edgePass 8/8)\n\nLOOP ITERATIONS NEEDED: 2 per candidate. Iteration 1: vocabulary alignment (note title must mirror agent query tokens). Iteration 2: completeness (overlay-save missed null-clear rule; locale-sum missed Intl parse pattern).\n\nINFRA BUGS FIXED ALONG THE WAY (required for loop to work):\n1. vec not persisted in note_created events → gate had no embeddings to score → always abstained\n2. supersedeNote() in-memory only → stale notes resurrected on daemon reload → gate margin collapsed\n3. embedStatus() stuck at loading → gate timed out\n4. Oracle leakage (grader in solve worktree) → OFF arm could read rubric\n\nKEY GATE LESSON: cosine alone insufficient inside a topical cluster. External-gap (note vocab ∩ query vocab / note vocab) was the discriminating signal. Margin collapses when stale duplicates exist — supersede aggressively. After fixes: margin 0.06→0.29, gate stable across restarts.\n\nCOMMIT: 2bc110f","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T13:59:29.079Z","vec":[-0.05255724862217903,-0.004994713701307774,-0.059609025716781616,0.011090177111327648